WEBVTT

00:02:58.954 --> 00:03:02.121
TB: We recommend you start
with: “Thank you for pointing that out.”

00:03:02.121 --> 00:03:04.579
It took courage for that person
to disrupt the bias,

00:03:04.621 --> 00:03:06.454
so it's important to acknowledge that.

00:03:06.454 --> 00:03:08.871
Then there are two choices
on what to say next.

00:03:08.913 --> 00:03:10.121
One, "I get it,"

00:03:10.121 --> 00:03:12.204
or two, "I don't get it.

00:03:12.204 --> 00:03:14.288
Could you explain
more after the meeting?"

00:03:14.329 --> 00:03:15.496
KS: The other day,

00:03:15.538 --> 00:03:17.913
you and I were recording
a podcast and I said,

00:03:17.913 --> 00:03:20.204
"HR serves three masters,"

00:03:20.246 --> 00:03:21.704
and you waved the purple flag.

00:03:21.746 --> 00:03:23.329
I knew what I had done wrong.

00:03:23.371 --> 00:03:25.746
Why was I using a slavery metaphor?

00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:27.079
We hit pause,

00:03:27.121 --> 00:03:29.163
I thanked you, and we rerecorded.

00:03:29.204 --> 00:03:30.496
It was no big deal.